      "parentID": "6179afc9220a9703c7e2f8e3",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "59a6f760be30701ad4d8a3b5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c|full_name}: Yeah I learned this is the big reason there *isn't* VRC for [insert platform here], even as a desktop/mobile client.\nUnity (the engine VRC is built upon) *has no concept of cross-platform assets.* And as VRC worlds & avatars are just unity asset packages, they have to be \"built\" and packaged, meaning they have to be done so *for each platform VRC supports*.\nEven if VRC made a dedicated effort for a Mac client, at this point it'd just be official worlds and Mac enthusiasts who'd use it.\nGranted, a Mac client could also potentially open up the door for an iOS client, as long as they use Metal APIs and build it as a universal app for iOS & Mac. — So you might get people on board just for that.\nBut the vast catalog of even Quest content would be unavailable out of the gate.\nMaybe in the future if \"SDK 4.0\" or what-have you introduces a custom \"universal\" asset format (tangentially similar to Udon and scripts).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
